  "name": "Fix PRView branch commit selectors",
  "pinned": false,
  "description": "# Conversation Summary\n\n1. **Problem Identified**: `PRCommitSelector` component was calling a non-existent `this.api.repo.commits()` method, causing API failures.\n\n2. **API Extension**: Added the missing `commits()` method to the API repo object with support for branch filtering and configurable limits.\n\n3. **Component Refactoring**: Rewrote `PRCommitSelector.vue` to properly handle two comparison modes (branch vs commit) with improved state management.\n\n4. **Props Fix**: Changed the API prop naming from `api` to `projectApi` for clarity and ensured proper API instance initialization through `initializeProjectContext()`.\n\n5. **Integration**: Updated `PRView.vue` to correctly pass the API instance to `PRCommitSelector` and implement the new commit comparison functionality.",
